  "label": "Hitler vanity stereotype",
  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that Adolf Hitler was vain or obsessed with his appearance, which is a historically inaccurate and offensive caricature. This stereotype is used to mock Hitler's perceived vanity by juxtaposing his image with manicured nails, implying he was obsessed with superficial beauty. This is a form of hate speech that trivializes the Holocaust and dehumanizes victims by associating the perpetrator with vanity.",
